==Trivia==
*Based on [[Possessed by Evil (Merciless)|Possessed by Evil]]'s Japanese name, Possessed by the Demon King, the one controlling Evil Emperor Cat may be [[Infernal Tyrant Nyandam]], whose Japanese name is Great Demon King Nyandam.
*If the first seven [[:Category:Advent Bosses|Advent Bosses]] are the Seven Deadly Sins, then Evil Emperor Cat may represent Judas, as he is a traitor to the Cat Army who became possessed by an analogue of Satan.
*There is a substantial amount of evidence to suggest that he was originally meant to be an [[Uncanny Legends]] boss who would unlock [[Emperor Cat (Legend Rare Cat)|Emperor Cat]] when defeated, acting as a counterpart to [[Li'l Nyandam (Special Cat)|Li'l Nyandam]].
**From [[Version 10.0 Update|Version 10.0]] to [[Version 10.2 Update|Version 10.2]], his ID was used by a placeholder enemy named コニャンダム亜種 ''Ko Nyandamu Ashu'' ("[[Li'l Nyandam (Enemy)|Li'l Nyandam]] Variant").
**[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]] and Possessed by Evil's [[Backgrounds|background]] were also added prematurely in 10.0, but Stone Cat was a placeholder [[:Category:Mythic Cats|Mythic Cat]] instead of a [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare Cat]] and the background had a different color scheme closer to that of [[Saint Red Fox]]. [[File:Bg147.png|thumb|right|Older Prelude to Ruin background]]
**[[Urs & Fenrir (Enemy)|Urs & Fenrir]] are a variant of [[Ururun Wolf (Enemy)|Ururun Wolf]], so [[PONOS Corporation|PONOS]] may have intended to keep this trend going with the other [[:Category:Mythic Cats|Mythic Cats]] from [[Legend Stages/SoL|Stories of Legend]].
**These placeholders were added in the same update as [[Dawn of the Beginning]], whose Japanese name is the opposite of [[Dead End Night]]'s. Dawn of the Beginning also comes 9 sub-chapters after [[Urs & Fenrir (Special Cat)|Urs & Fenrir]] in [[The Gelatin Mines]], which was 9 sub-chapters after [[Depths of My Heart]].
**Emperor Cat has the same range, movement speed and slow chance as allied Li'l Nyandam while Evil Emperor Cat's Omni Strike gives him the same reach as enemy Li'l Nyandam.
**Evil Emperor Cat is a [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]], the same trait as all Uncanny Legends drops.
**Before [[Possessed Empress]] was introduced, Evil Emperor Cat stood out as the only [[:Category:Advent Bosses|Advent Boss]] to be the enemy version of a [[Cat Units|Cat Unit]]. Likewise, Emperor Cat is to this day the only [[:Category:Legend Rare Cats|Legend Rare Cat]] to have an enemy counterpart.
*Prior to the [[Version 10.2 Update|Version 10.2.1 Update]], he had a Level 3 [[Surge Attack]] with a distance of 150~255, lasting for 60f.
*Since they were only released one update apart, it is possible that he is the titular "Dark Lord" of [[Dark Lord's Decree]].
*His attack stat resembles the well-known [[wikipedia:Number of the beast|Number of the Beast]].

